WEBVTT

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:37.860
For the fourth batter, I made
Mihashi shake off the sign.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.660
Made him?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.790
Then a shoot to the outside that turned into a ball.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:45.910
The third pitch was the same as the second, a fastball.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.040
And you have a sign to make him shake you off?

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.040
Crap.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.550
We just came up with it.

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.630
It seemed like they were reading my mix of pitches,

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.090
so I thought it would fake them out a bit.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:59.340
Mihashi just nods at everything, so...

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.430
Yeah, at everything.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:02.930
He just nods...

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:03.930
at everything!?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.230
Oh, you were here?

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.770
Now that he mentions it, I've never seen Mihashi shake off a sign before.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.980
Was he just leaving it all up to the catcher?

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.820
I'll have to give him some lessons about that.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.160
I'll have to do it after the game.

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.700
If I frighten the pitcher now, it'll cause problems for Abe.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.290
Getting the fourth batter out was big, huh?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.160
Uh, yes.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.000
Let's keep it up for the last four innings!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.850
Yes!

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.590
Pitch like I tell you to.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.970
The reason Mihashi doesn't shake me off is because I told him not to, right at the start.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:40.630
That was a bad thing to tell a pitcher.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.050
Pitchers have the right to shake off signs!

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:46.640
Right now, even if I tell him to shake me off, he won't.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.390
Mihashi.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.440
Nice pitching to the last batter.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.270
I-It's thanks to you, Abe.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:58.280
Because I pitch like you tell me to.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:58.950
Yeah.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.990
See? This guy isn't dissatisfied with anything right now.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.700
I'm also drinking water. I haven't forgotten.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.460
There's no need to change anything.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:16.550
Replacing the pitcher, Takenouchi, is number 10, Kashima.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:21.840
Replacing the left fielder, Kitamura, is Takenouchi.

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.510
Bottom of the fifth inning. Nishiura High to bat.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:25.850
At his best, Bijou's second pitcher is 10 km/h faster than Takenouchi.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:29.770
First batter. Center fielder: Number 8, Izumi.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.440
We'll have to survive a full rotation with that 10 km/h difference.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.230
Ready!

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.730
Play!

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:41.200
Ball.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.360
Take it easy.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:47.580
This guy doesn't pitch first, despite his speed,
because he's not consistent.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.580
In the beginning, he doesn't throw fast,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.080
and the difference between strikes and balls is obvious.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.170
If it's in the box, I'll hit it with all my might!

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.960
Good one, Izumi!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:02.970
Ball!

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:05.850
Takumi's starting poorly today as well?

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:08.930
No matter how much he warms up in the bullpen, it doesn't matter.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.980
Let's draw out his power with two sliders.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:16.400
Until my engine revs up,
I want to go with fastballs.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.570
Ball!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:23.030
See? If I can't get a fastball in,
then a breaking ball won't work either.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.410
Pitcher! Swing your arm.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.490
Naomasa understands.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.410
Why doesn't Takeshi?

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:31.700
I won't wait, even though it's 3-1.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.620
I'll swing hard and drive through the infield!

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.840
One, two!

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.920
Nice batting!

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:40.760
All right!

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.050
Nice batting!

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:42.720
Thanks.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.380
Did you do <i>that</i> ?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.590
I didn't.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:47.640
I'm only nervous during my first at-bat.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.260
I see.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.390
When it's your turn, I'll do it for you again.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.850
I'll hold you to that.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.020
First!

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.190
Ball!

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.900
Why are you throwing so hard?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.110
Ease up on the heat and get a strike with a slider.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.950
Right down the middle would be fine.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:09.740
No.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:13.700
You rascal. I'm trying to help you warm up.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.000
That's right. First base is open and all.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.710
Let me throw hard.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.340
If you do that, my engine will rev right up!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.010
All right!

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.380
It dropped in left field!

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.640
One out, runners on first and third, and now the cleanup hitter?

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.260
First and third have to guard the line against an extra-base hit.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.850
Second and short will come in a bit to prepare for a double play.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:39.560
Of course. No one wants them to score a fourth run.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:40.690
Fourth batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Tajima.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:44.320
To limit them to three runs, we have to maintain those fielding positions.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.820
At worst, a sacrifice fly.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.450
With one out, and runners on first and third,
I'd like to bring Hanai up to bat.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:52.870
In order to hold them to three runs, we have to stop the cleanup hitter.

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.540
Is there nothing I can do except lean outside and let him throw what he likes?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:03.210
Even a ball would be okay,
but at least get it in the box.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.550
Although the cleanup batter usually connects, he can't hit long.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:10.260
Even if he connects, they'll only score a run, unless he hits to a bad spot.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.890
I'll warm up my arm on the cleanup hitter.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.770
Low and outside... In there!

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:15.810
Not good enough!

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:18.770
It's between first and second!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.690
The third run!

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.950
Takumi! It's time to get serious!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.200
If you throw hard, they won't hit it so easily!

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.330
It's tough yelling from the outfield.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:36.870
Well, Takeshi will properly...

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.790
Fifth batter. Right fielder: Number 9, Hanai.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.420
Hey! He's not going to talk to Takumi?

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.710
Ready!

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.750
With this, it's a two-run difference.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.670
I'll take a sacrifice fly.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.720
We need to score more runs
before the pitcher warms up!

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.550
If Hanai scores a run, we'll be able to win!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.310
I won't crumble!

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.060
I'll drive in the fourth run!

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:00.770
It's a fly ball!

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:02.980
Go!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:06.940
The fourth run!

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.660
Come on. If you get Takumi going, he can pitch better than Yoshito.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.160
Don't let him give away hits one after another, Takeshi.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.580
Takumi!

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.210
I should've asked for a ball on the first pitch just now.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.170
Sorry.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.710
Y-Yeah.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.050
Your arm should be warmed up by now, right?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.300
Your pitches were flying in the bullpen today too.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.880
If you're warmed up,
they won't get any more hits.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.800
Bring it on!

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:36.640
Nice!

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.260
A fourth run!

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:38.140
Good going!

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:39.310
Yeah!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.730
Don't look so happy over something like that.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:48.650
He scored the fourth run.

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:50.320
Sixth batter. First baseman: Number 3, Oki.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.200
Now, it's not Abe's fault anymore.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.910
Strike!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.490
Oh! Feels good.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.540
After giving away two runs, he got one in.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:00.910
Strike.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.080
He did a good job of talking to the pitcher.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:05.290
If it were me, what would I have said?

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:08.460
Strike!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.630
Should I go back to prep school?

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.760
If I stay here,

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.760
it'll bring back memories that give me heartburn.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:19.100
I'll end up unable to move for days.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:26.230
Strike!

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:31.650
Out!

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.030
Let's go back.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:37.570
Bathroom.

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.780
Right...

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:42.580
You should've gone during ground maintenance after the fifth inning.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.290
Roka went to the bathroom.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:49.340
He'll be right back, so don't freeze up like that.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.380
It can't be helped.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:53.090
I'll wait until Roka gets back.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.430
Thank you.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.720
Ah, that's right.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:00.680
Mihashi.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.680
If Kashima hits you, you'll be in serious trouble.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:06.480
Don't take a dead ball as a way to get on base!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.190
Bottom of the sixth inning.
Nishiura High School to bat.

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:12.780
All right, Abe. Get on base. I'll follow up.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:13.570
Seventh batter. Catcher: Number 2, Abe.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:14.860
Mizutani.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.200
What about <i>that</i> ?
Seventh batter. Catcher: Number 2, Abe.

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.570
Please do it!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:23.040
That's what I said to Mihashi, but honestly,
I want to get on base even if it means getting hit!

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.000
Strike!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.460
It's fast.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.920
Ball!

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:36.880
Crap. I didn't take a single swing!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.220
Nice positioning.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:39.800
That was good just now.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:42.970
Takumi threw a slider without complaining.

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:46.600
Ball!

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.810
Okay! Okay!

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:52.570
Being this wild is good.

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.280
Don't say "wild"!

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.360
All right. It's a showdown with the batter.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.910
Eighth batter. Left fielder: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:09:59.780
Ready!

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.950
I'll try and make them say "Nice batting" again.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:05.290
Strike!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.210
How fast was that just now?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:07.920
Nice ball!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.880
He can't reach 140 km/h, so it's slower than the machine, right?

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.500
But when a person is throwing it...

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:14.880
Strike!

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.840
It's scary!

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:17.300
Swing, Mizutani!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.300
Uh, oh. This looks bad.
Swing, Mizutani!

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.550
You won't connect unless you swing.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.560
"Nice batting" Mizutani, switch on!

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.020
I'm too nervous. I don't feel ticklish at all.

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.480
Strike!

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:31.400
That was really high.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:32.610
You were close!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.730
He's faster than he was last inning.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.230
Mihashi.

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:39.570
The way we swing, we have to start the moment he throws.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.950
The moment?

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.580
Don't get hit. You'll break a bone.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.830
What's wrong, Mr. Nice Batting?

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:45.700
Shut up!

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.370
Thanks.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.540
Me? Why? Did I hear wrong?

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.250
I'm happy that he's worried about me.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.670
Ninth batter. Pitcher: Number 1, Mihashi.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:57.090
People worry about me because I'm useful.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.510
Mihashi can't possibly hit off this guy.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:05.010
A bunt. In order to be useful,
I have to be careful and not get injured.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:08.060
This guy's a pitcher, and he's left-handed.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.140
If it's inside, he'd better dodge.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:11.600
Inside and high!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:12.400
Ball!

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.310
An amazing sound.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.570
Strike!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.440
It can't be helped if Mihashi strikes out trying to bunt.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.450
Bunt... I have to bring Izumi up with two outs and a runner on second.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.410
We're going to score...

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.700
two more runs.

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.040
Strong!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:30.830
Second!

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.380
Out!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:36.590
Yeah!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:39.130
That ball was difficult.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.680
Don't worry about it. There'll be other chances!

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.640
Y-Yeah.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:48.390
Oh, he's still all right.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.520
Th-Thank you.

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.690
Oh? Sure.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.940
Hey! Don't go out like that!

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.650
You're supposed to drink water every inning, right!?

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:02.650
Don't forget!

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:03.860
That's right!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.450
I'm happy.

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.790
Even though I failed to bunt, he's still worried about me.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.410
Okay. Let's go!

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.080
Yeah!

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:16.840
He's worried about me because I can get outs when I pitch.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.670
It's all thanks to Abe.

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.380
His pitch count is... twelve?

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.760
Considering he walked a guy, I guess twelve is all right.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.890
Walking someone is never good.

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:31.100
Yano, why don't you try
praising people for a change?

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:32.350
You're too soft, Captain.

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.350
But well, nice pitching.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:38.440
If you try any more risky plays at the plate, I'll tell the coach to bring you in.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:43.610
The coach is already a bit suspicious
about all the rough plays till now.

00:12:43.610 --> 00:12:47.680
Plus, if Yano says something to the coach, I'll probably be replaced then and there.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:50.040
Don't forget your role.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:54.960
If I don't follow the coach's signs,
I'll be removed from the starting lineup.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:58.080
If I'll be removed whether or not I play rough, then...

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:59.960
it'd be better not to.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.510
Watanabe, a player I ran into during a practice game with Yokohama Shinmei,

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.800
didn't make the Kanagawa tournament.

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:10.100
As for Kimura from Samadai Gyouda, whom we played in the third round...

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:13.640
After the tournament, I should check on his injury.

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.610
Even if he's all healed up,
what I did was unforgivable.

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:23.320
Watanabe, Kimura, I'm going to quit baseball after high school.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:26.780
Just for today, let me work hard for these guys.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.620
Father and Mother are also in the stands now.

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.750
If I said I was going to quit, they'd probably cry.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:33.910
They put in a lot of time and money for my sake.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:37.000
Top of the seventh inning.
Bijouda Sayama High to bat.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.380
I'm... an idiot. I'm really sorry.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:42.750
Eighth batter. Catcher: Number 2, Kurata.

00:13:42.750 --> 00:13:43.920
Ready!

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:48.090
A curveball down the middle.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:49.890
Ball!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.430
Swing! Swing!

00:13:52.010 --> 00:13:52.720
No swing!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.480
He really is shaking off the sign.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.690
But you can't change a battery's dynamics so easily.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.150
If they're planning to finish with a fastball, then the next will be a breaking ball too.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.610
If that's the case, they'd better avoid pitching inside where I like it.

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.200
They really don't want to put a runner on base and bring up Kou,

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.740
who's hit safely three times.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.660
At a time like this, the catcher can only plan for the worst case scenario.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:19.790
Following his basic mix of pitches, it'll be a slider to the outside!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:20.830
He figured it out!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.250
All right! Between left and center!

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:24.840
All right!

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:30.840
Strike!

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.260
One out!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.640
Outfield, possible play at the plate!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:35.600
First batter. Shortstop: Number 6, Kawashima.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.180
We'll go with fastballs.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.100
We'll get two outs without letting the runner advance.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:40.520
Ready!

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:44.520
Now, he'll probably throw his finishing pitch as hard as he can.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:46.990
Show it to me.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:49.570
Strike!

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.660
Even though it was in the strike zone, he let it pass.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.370
He's closing his eyes.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.990
Is he visualizing the last pitch?

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.750
It's the first time Kawashima has seen the fastball,

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:00.370
but it was almost like he was waiting for it.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.830
Well, it's the seventh inning.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.340
We'll stop them using just the fastball!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.590
I'll bet that the next pitch is also a fastball.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:07.340
Concentrate.

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:09.010
Carefully...

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:09.800
A safety bunt?

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:12.930
Well done! He totally killed it.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:13.550
Shit!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.600
First, throw to first!

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:14.970
Yes!

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:17.180
Safe!

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.140
Kou! Nice running!

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:22.440
Third runner!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.020
Yano.

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:25.520
Stay sharp!

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.110
Mihashi!

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.450
One out. Runners on first and third with the second batter at the plate.

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.320
Watch out for a squeeze.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:34.910
It'd be great if we could read them well, but...

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.990
If you hesitate on the throw home, I'll kill you!

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:38.500
Yes!

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.580
One run would be big here.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.080
I can't hold back.

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:42.960
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Ishikawa.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.380
Abe won't get injured.

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:46.420
Second batter. Third baseman: Number 5, Ishikawa.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:49.130
If there's a squeeze, I'll stop it even if I have to get hurt.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.470
Be sure to do it this time, Tetsurou!

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.340
We'll pitch the first ball outside.

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:02.230
A fastball.

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:05.860
A fastball on the outside high corner, a strike.

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.900
If they're trying a squeeze,
then I have to make the bunt fail!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:09.570
Okay!

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:10.780
Strike!

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.910
And now, there's no chance of a double play.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.870
The next one will really be the real deal.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.830
Throw it far outside.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:23.790
To a spot that the batter can't reach, but Abe can.

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.250
There... I'll aim there!

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:30.800
The runners are on the move!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.470
All right, we're on the money!

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:33.630
Hit it, Tetsurou!

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:35.510
He hit it!

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:38.810
Oki! Grab it!

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:39.680
You're in my way!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:40.720
Abe!

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:41.430
It slipped!

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:47.520
Shit! I'll step on him!

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:53.610
Safe!

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:55.070
B-Ball!

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.410
Third... First...

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.540
Abe! Time out!

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:09.170
Time out!

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:10.090
What happened?

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.380
Can you stand?

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:13.760
I'm fine.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:14.510
Ready!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:15.090
Hey!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:16.300
Is it bad?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.930
No, I'm fine.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.640
I'm sorry. I threw it to a weird spot.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.390
I said I'm fine!

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:26.850
Oki, it's all right. Go throw the ball around.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.400
What? Why!?

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.070
Excuse me. Is it all right to take an injury timeout?

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.150
Mihashi, let's get him back to the bench.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:38.030
Mihashi!

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:38.870
Yes!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.160
Okay. Support his waist.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.040
Grab his belt. His belt.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.120
Okay? One, two...

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.450
Takeshi.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.580
It wasn't me! Just now...

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:49.170
I know. I saw it up close.

00:17:49.170 --> 00:17:51.210
He caught the ball in a bad position.

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:51.960
Don't get hooked!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:54.920
More importantly, didn't he step on your arm?

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.880
Oh. The spikes only grazed me a bit.

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.800
Crap! That's pretty deep.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.430
You'd better go and have it looked at properly.

00:18:01.430 --> 00:18:02.140
Yeah.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:07.770
An announcement to the spectators.
Please wait while Abe's injury is treated.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.650
You've sprained your knee. It hurts, right?

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.770
No, it doesn't.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:15.940
It's a sprain, right?

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.990
Will you tape it up for me?

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:19.450
Abe, can you stand?

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.740
Come on, where's your fighting spirit!

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.660
You're not putting any weight on your left foot.

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.590
If you can't put your foot down,
it's a second degree sprain, or worse.

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:36.090
Plus, if you try moving now,
you'll make the injury worse.

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.470
Most importantly, it hurts so much you can't squat, right?

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:39.090
I can do it!

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.510
You can't.

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.890
It took you that long just to stand.
What're you saying?

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.930
Tajima, put on protective gear.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:46.470
Yes!

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:48.230
Nishihiro, left field.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.600
Mizutani, third base. Okay?

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:50.230
Yes!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.110
Go to the outfield and start throwing the ball around immediately.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:54.070
Yes!

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:58.070
Mihashi, go back to the mound for some toss-and-catch too.

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.400
Mihashi!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:23.800
A-Abe. Sit down.

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:26.140
Y-You need to ice it.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.190
Um...

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.690
Don't worry. We'll give him proper medical treatment.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:45.160
I'll get... two more outs.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.670
Even if Abe is gone, I'll...

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.630
Okay!

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:02.880
Tajima!

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:05.890
I'll be signaling for strikes and balls.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:08.350
But the rest is up to you,
because you're close to the batter.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.350
Nishiura High, announcing a change in positions.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:10.140
Okay

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:11.600
It's up to you!

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:12.560
Yes!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:16.190
Replacing the catcher, Abe, is Tajima.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:19.730
Replacing the third baseman, Tajima, is Mizutani.

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:22.570
Replacing the left fielder, Mizutani, is Nishihiro.

00:20:22.570 --> 00:20:24.410
Abe's out?

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.620
He sprained his knee!
Fourth batter. Catcher: Number 5, Tajima.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.990
It's not serious, is it?
Fourth batter. Catcher: Number 5, Tajima.

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:29.620
Seventh batter. Left fielder: Number 10, Nishihiro.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.950
They said he was okay.

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.750
All right. He's okay! He's okay!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:34.040
Eighth batter. Third baseman: Number 7, Mizutani.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.790
Oki, don't worry about it anymore.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:37.340
Y-Yeah...

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:38.290
I can't hear you!

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:40.130
That's all changes.

00:20:40.130 --> 00:20:42.340
Ball back!

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:43.510
Tajima!

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:48.350
It's Tajima.

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.220
Sorry for making you wait!

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:54.100
Fastball. Curveball. Shoot. Slider.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.980
Inside. Outside. High. Low.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:58.270
Down the middle and full speed. Okay?

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:00.020
O-Okay.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:01.570
Mihashi, give me your hand.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.110
I'm the one who's more scared?

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:09.660
I wish we'd teamed up during a practice game.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:11.660
I'll catch by sheer willpower if necessary.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:14.620
But I'm not completely confident about being a catcher.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:19.380
Things won't be the same without Abe,
but I'll do my best!

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:23.010
T-Tajima... rely on me!

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.300
Okay! I will!

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:31.470
Oki! Let me hear you yell! Abe's fine!

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:32.970
Okay!

00:21:33.470 --> 00:21:38.020
One out! Infield, double play!
Outfield, possible play at the plate!

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.770
Third! There's no need to rush the throw.

00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.360
If you do it properly, it'll get there in time!

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:44.820
Okay!

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:47.820
Nishihiro! I'm counting on you as usual!

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:49.200
Okay!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:51.830
Let's hear it!

00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:54.040
Yeah!

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:59.000
Even Tajima thinks like that.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.460
I'm not the only one who's uneasy.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:05.380
Abe is the team's regular catcher.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:10.140
We'll work hard to make up for Abe's absence.

00:23:43.560 --> 00:23:46.770
An emergency that no one had foreseen.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:51.650
Abe, who'd always been there, is injured for the first time.

00:23:51.650 --> 00:23:58.450
In the end, will the battery of Mihashi and Tajima work against Bijoudai Sayama?

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:01.790
And it's Nishihiro's debut as left fielder.

00:24:02.920 --> 00:24:03.920
Next episode:

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:05.170
Because I'm the Ace.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:07.800
"RICE" is not rice.
